{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Offline re-score of the recorded live run against the corrected false-accept bar\n\nZero model calls. Re-scored `src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/provider_parity_results.json` through\n`provider_parity.recheck_recorded`, before and after the fix.\n\n### Correction chosen: keep the name, fix the computation\n\n`false_accept` is now `blocked / safe` (the false-positive rate over gold-safe items), NOT\n`not-blocked / safe`. Both comparison directions (`parity.py` non-inferiority rise check and the\n`max_false_accept` ceiling) are UNCHANGED — they were already written for an error rate. Cited\ngrounds that this is the meaning the repo already holds: `src/rebar/llm/evals/eval.py:399,491`\n(`false_accept = wrongly-fired / must-not-fire`, computed as `fp / n_nofire`);\n`docs/plan-review-gate.md:382` release threshold `false_accept: 0.0`;\n`src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/plan-review-container.eval.yaml:75` \"candidate false-accept rises by\n<= 2pp\"; and `parity.py`'s own `max_false_accept: float = 0.10` default.\n\nDirect evidence the old computation made the ceiling always-fail: the new prerequisite test, run\nagainst the UNFIXED source, produced `prerequisite false acceptance 1.000 exceeds 0.100` on a\ncandidate that wrongly blocked ZERO safe items.\n\n### Per-slot verdict, before vs after\n\n| slot | metric | before | after |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| standard | false_accept v1 -> v2 | 0.786 -> 0.786 (PASS) | 0.214 -> 0.214 (PASS) |\n| standard | other failures | 1 decision flip | 1 decision flip |\n| frontier | false_accept v1 -> v2 | 0.786 -> 0.929, **FAIL** \"rose 0.143\" | 0.214 -> 0.071, **PASS** |\n| frontier | other failures | agreement 0.929 < 0.95; 2 flips | agreement 0.929 < 0.95; 2 flips |\n\nValidity 1.000/1.000, error rate 0.000, n_gold 28 on both slots, unchanged.\n\n**The frontier false-accept failure CLEARS.** Under the corrected metric Bedrock's false-positive\nrate on gold-safe items is 0.071 vs direct Anthropic's 0.214 — a 14.3pp IMPROVEMENT, which the old\ninverted computation reported as a 14.3pp regression. That is the two gold-ADVISORY cases\n(`FP-rename-all-callsites-updated`, `FP-create-index-concurrently`) Anthropic false-fired on and\nBedrock did not.\n\n### What still fails — the bar is NOT met\n\nBoth slots still fail. Standard: 1 decision flip. Frontier: 2 decision flips plus verdict agreement\n0.929 below the 0.95 floor. No reinterpretation of the bar is offered; as written it is unmet."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785720646272922001,"uuid":"2186ffb6-2a12-42d5-a811-cb1b8a5d2bbd"}